      "alt": "SANTA CRUZ SENTINEL-DEWS\n\nAuthorities Impose Ban On 'Rock And Roll' Dances Here\n\nAuthorities have imposed a ban on \"rock and roll\" and other fren- zied forms of terpsichore in Santa Cruz as a result of \"obscene and highly suggestive dancing\" by teen-agers at an affair held at civic auditorium Saturday night.\n\nPolice halted the dance and sent some 200 teen-agers home after observing a number of the couples engaging in \"highly sug- gestive, stimulating and tantaliz- ing motions\" induced by the pro- vocative rhythms of an all-Negro band.\n\nThe dance, scheduled for 9 a.m. to 1 a.m., was stopped at 12:20 a.m.\n\nThe music \"excited the crowd to passion at times and it was feared the crowd might become uncontrollable,\" Lieut. Richard Overton noted in a report to Po- lice Chief Al Huntsman.\n\nHuntsman said he \"absolutely\" agreed with Overton's action in ending the affair and dispersing the crowd.\n\nDances of this type will not be tolerated in the future \"anywhere in Santa Cruz,\" Huntsman said.\n\nAuditorium Manager Ray Judah said the band le ader had been told he will not be permit- ted to plav the auditorium again.\n\n\"He's through,\" said Judah. The same organization play- ed at civic auditorium last month and there were no repercussions that time.\n\nOverton, who had been instruct- ed by Huntsman to \"keep an eye\" on the affair, reported that most of the teen-agers were from out- side Santa Cruz, many of them from Watsonville.\n\nThere was no suggestion that liquor or a \"roughhouse\" disturb- ance was involved-only the sug- gestive acrobatics of some of the dancers.\n\nAnd Overton's report pointed out that only a minority of those attending indulged in objection- able dancing.\n\nSeveral co uples, apparently driven to abandon by the music, were observed behaving in a sug- gestive manner. Other dancers formed a circle around the exhi- bitionists in an apparent effort to screen them from the officers' view.\n\nHowever, the participants \"ap- parently became oblivious to the officers' presence",
